| #742 (/retry guessed the tool name from the error text) | Fixed. /retry now uses the tool name the prompt loop records (resolve_retry_tool, src/commands_retry.rs:120) and only scans the error text if no name was recorded. Every place that stores an error stores the tool name with it (dispatch.rs:1182,1223,1242, repl.rs:696,732), and every place that clears the error clears the name too. | The two tests for this each ran by name: 1 passed each. One of them uses an error message where the text scan picks the wrong tool, and the recorded name correctly wins. |
| #958 (the unhittable count was saved without its denominator) | Fixed. Both places that write this to the ledger pass in the value count_unhittable_surprises_with_git computes, not a hand-typed number. | The unhittable module's tests: 66 passed. Some of them build the count from real ledger rows. |
| #959 (daily_diary.sh spent tokens without recording them) | Fixed. A later session did the work this receipt failed to do. The script sets YOYO_AUDIT=1 (line 175), and report_diary_spend() prints the run's spend on stderr (line 199). If there is no usage record it says so instead of printing zero (line 203). | Line numbers cited from the file at HEAD. |
| #960 ("Self-improvement" fallback task) | Closed as not planned. It was a generic fallback task with no goal to check. Its log tail shows the Day 211 provider/model misconfiguration, and the agent made no changes. | The issue body. |

